# 2026-11-04 D-552, one by-hand row on Google's lab Galaxy S26 units (Developer Device Platform pool m1q-36,
# SM-S942U1; android/ddp/devices.json), not a page row: the campaign name holds no `dashboard`, so the team page never
# reads it as a weekly sitting, and the lab units' weekly stand-in rows stay the s26-ddp slot's.
# litert-community/Qwen3.5-0.8B (Qwen3.5-0.8B_int8.litertlm, Hub main LFS sha256 25447e25..., 964,566,992 B) on the
# LiteRT team's protocol row, native-benchmark-1024x256 = litert_lm_advanced_main --benchmark, prefill forced to exactly
# 1024 tokens, decode 256, context 2048 (methodology/agreed-protocol-gemma4.md "The spec"), LiteRT-LM GPU on the side
# build v0.19.0-pregpu (commit 771b06e1 = the flat pin's, with Google's prebuilt libLiteRtGpuAccelerator.so loaded at
# run time; android/engine-pins.json litert-lm.v0.19.0-pregpu, engine_version v0.19.0).
# This row = matrices/d543-qwen35-s26-gpu-pregpu-android.cells' row (the attached Galaxy S26 SM-S942Q, 2026-11-04)
# with runs=3 instead of runs=1: one Device Run job = three launches on one lab unit, one benchmark per process,
# the wrapper's 120 s cooldown and thermal gate before runs 2 and 3; run 1 builds the GPU program cache (firstEver).
# The two other builds of the round are their own files and campaigns (engine-build= is not part of the cell key, so
# two rows that differ only in it are one duplicate cell): matrices/d552-qwen35-ddp-s26-flat-android.cells and
# matrices/d552-qwen35-ddp-s26-public-android.cells.
# Run: BENCH_DDP_ALL_RUNTIMES=1 ./bench matrix <this file> --ddp m1q-36 --campaign 2026-11-04-d552-qwen35-ddp-s26-pregpu
# (run_ddp wires a row's engine-build= only under that switch; without it the row is skipped as
# side-build-not-wired-on-ddp).
android litert-lm litert-community/Qwen3.5-0.8B native-benchmark-1024x256 backend=gpu engine-build=v0.19.0-pregpu file=Qwen3.5-0.8B_int8.litertlm context-tokens=2048 runs=3
